Hi,
         I am using Ubuntu 9.04 Jaunty Jackalope with the latest alsa-driver
snapshot provided by Takashi. The sound system does not work without a
hda-verb command manually executed every time the system starts up. The
command I execute is:

hda-verb /dev/snd/hwC0D0 0x15 SET_EAPD_BTLENABLE 2

If I do this I get audio out. But my internal mic does not work and nor does
jack sensing. When I insert a device into the headphone jack the speakers do
not get muted and there is also no sound from the headphones themselves.
Even an external mic/line-in device does not work. I have attached the
output of alsa-info.sh here.. Please go through it and try to solve the
problem.

Thanks and Regards,
Karthik

